<section class="about inner grid-section reveal" id="about">
  <header class="section-head"><p class="section-index">01 / About</p><p class="section-aside">Systems thinker.<br />Product-minded builder.</p></header>
  <div class="about-grid"><h2>Engineering for the<br /><em>real world.</em></h2><div class="about-copy"><p>I’m a senior engineer focused on scalable full stack systems and practical AI. Over four years in cybersecurity SaaS, I’ve built platforms that serve hundreds of enterprise tenants and process millions of security records.</p><p>My work sits at the intersection of <a href="#expertise">distributed infrastructure</a>, <a href="#expertise">safe automation</a>, and products people can actually use—from vulnerability remediation agents to a privacy-first suite of 31 browser tools.</p></div></div>
</section>
<section class="work inner grid-section reveal" id="work">
  <header class="section-head"><p class="section-index">02 / Selected work</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/suryanshp1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">147 repositories ↗</a></header>
  <div class="section-intro"><h2>Things I’ve<br /><em>made real.</em></h2><p>A selection of products and infrastructure—designed for usefulness, scale, and a long life after launch.</p></div>
  <article class="project project-featured"><a class="project-visual owl" href="https://www.owlutil.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="Visit Owl Util"><div class="browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>owlutil.com</span></div><div class="owl-stage"><span class="owl-mark">◉</span><p>Free online tools<br />for every task.</p><div class="tool-pills"><span>JSON</span><span>Regex</span><span>SQL</span><span>+28</span></div></div></a><div class="project-copy"><div class="project-meta"><span>Flagship product</span><span>Live · 2026</span></div><h3>Owl Util</h3><p class="project-kicker">31 useful tools. Zero accounts. Your data stays yours.</p><p>A fast, privacy-first collection for developers, creators, and curious people. Every tool is immediately usable, free, and built to process data locally whenever possible.</p><div class="tags"><span>Astro</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>Browser APIs</span><span>Product</span></div><a class="project-link" href="https://www.owlutil.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit product <b>↗</b></a></div></article>
  <article class="project project-reverse"><div class="project-copy"><div class="project-meta"><span>Developer tool</span><span>Open source</span></div><h3>Advanced<br />Coding CLI</h3><p class="project-kicker">An agentic coding companion that lives in the terminal.</p><p>A capable CLI agent with model context protocol support and an interactive terminal interface—built to understand a codebase, plan changes, and help ship them.</p><div class="tags"><span>Python</span><span>LLMs</span><span>MCP</span><span>TUI</span></div><a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/suryanshp1/advance-coding-cli-agent" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the code <b>↗</b></a></div><a class="project-visual terminal" href="https://github.com/suryanshp1/advance-coding-cli-agent" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="View Advanced Coding CLI on GitHub"><div class="terminal-head"><span>● ● ●</span><small>agent — ~/project</small></div><pre><code><span class="muted">$</span> advance <span class="accent">build</span>

<span class="muted">→</span> Reading repository context
<span class="muted">→</span> Mapping dependencies
<span class="muted">→</span> Creating implementation plan

<span class="success">✓</span> Ready to make changes
<span class="cursor">▋</span></code></pre></a></article>
  <article class="project cdc-project"><a class="project-visual cdc-visual" href="https://github.com/suryanshp1/simple-cdc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" aria-label="View Simple CDC on GitHub"><div class="cdc-top"><span>POSTGRESQL</span><span>CHANGE STREAM</span><span>CONSUMER</span></div><div class="cdc-flow" aria-hidden="true"><div class="db-node"><i></i><strong>DB</strong><small>source</small></div><div class="event-track"><span style="--i:0">INSERT</span><span style="--i:1">UPDATE</span><span style="--i:2">DELETE</span><span style="--i:3">UPDATE</span></div><div class="db-node sink"><i></i><strong>API</strong><small>services</small></div></div><div class="cdc-log"><span>00:01:42.083</span><b>event captured</b><span>offset 024891</span></div></a><div class="project-copy"><div class="project-meta"><span>Distributed systems</span><span>Open source · 2026</span></div><h3>Simple CDC</h3><p class="project-kicker">Database changes, captured and streamed in near real time.</p><p>A lightweight Change Data Capture pipeline with asynchronous event processing for reliable synchronization between distributed services. It demonstrates service decoupling, event-driven communication, and eventual consistency in a focused, inspectable system.</p><div class="tags"><span>Python</span><span>PostgreSQL</span><span>Event-driven</span><span>Async</span></div><a class="project-link" href="https://github.com/suryanshp1/simple-cdc" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the code <b>↗</b></a></div></article>
</section>
<section class="experience inner grid-section reveal" id="experience">
